      "id": 1,
      "text": "Charleston was once called Kreischerville after Balthasar Kreischer, whose 1854 brick factory sparked the area’s growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charleston%2C_Staten_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The surviving Kreischer House at 4500 Arthur Kill Road was renovated and now can host a 70‑seat restaurant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charleston%2C_Staten_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Charleston borders the Arthur Kill, a tidal strait that separates Staten Island from New Jersey.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charleston%2C_Staten_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s name likely honors Charles Kreischer, a son of Balthasar, rather than the earlier Androvette family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charleston%2C_Staten_Island"
    },
    {
